export endnote Endnote (file)\nexport refworks Refworks\n\n[Cover]\n[Add this title to your marked items list]\nAdd\nJarring III.\nAuthor: \tJones, Mirabelle, artist.\nPublished: \t[Rosendale, New York ; Los Angeles, California ; Berkeley, California] : [Mirabelle Jones], [2013-2014]\nDescription: \t3 volumes : illustrations ; 14-24 cm, in box 25 x 18 x 7 cm\nFormat: \tBook\nSummary:\n\"Jarring III is a set of three letterpress printed & hand-bound artists' books in an edition of 50 that seek to end the silence and stigma surrounding sexual assault and rape by sharing the narratives of 22 survivors. The goals of the project are as follows: Promote discourse and awareness about sexual assault in our communities; Speak out about sexual assault by sharing the experiences of sexual assault survivors; Create a publicly accessible archive of survivor experiences for research and therapeutic use; Raise funds for Rape Crisis Centers (RCCs) and survivor resources through book sales and donations.\" -- From artist's website, viewed February 21, 2017. http://www.mirabellejones.com/jarring-a-book-arts-campaign-for-social-change/ ... ( see more )\n\n    Subjects\n    Location\n    MARC\n    Full Record\n\nSubjects\nRape victims in art.\nRape in art.\nArtists' books -- United States -- Specimens.\nArtists' books -- New York (State) -- Rosendale -- 21st century.\nArtists' books -- California -- Los Angeles -- 21st century.\nArtists' books -- California -- Berkeley -- 21st century.\nArtists' books -- 2013.\nArtists' books -- 2014.\nCut-paper work.\nAccordion fold format (Binding)\n\nVarying Title: \tJarring 3\nJarring three\nLocation\nOnline\nLocation \tCall # \tStatus \tNotes\nArt Library Artists' Book Collection \tN7433.4.J634 J37 2013 \tIn Transit \tUNC copy: No. 23 of 50\nMARC\nLEADER 00000cam a2200565Ii 4500 \n001    973339209 \n003    OCoLC \n005    20170519011655.0 \n008    170221m20132014nyua          000 0 eng d \n035    (OCoLC)973339209 \n040    CUY|beng|erda|cCUY|dCUY|dOCLCF|dNOC \n043    n-us--- \n049    NOCC \n050  4 N7433.4.J634|bJ37 2013 \n100 1  Jones, Mirabelle,|eartist. \n245 10 Jarring III. \n246 3  Jarring 3 \n246 3  Jarring three \n264  1 [Rosendale, New York ;|aLos Angeles, California ;\n       |aBerkeley, California] :|b[Mirabelle Jones],|c[2013-2014]\n300    3 volumes :|billustrations ;|c14-24 cm, in box 25 x 18 x 7\n       cm \n336    text|btxt|2rdacontent \n337    unmediated|bn|2rdamedia \n338    volume|bnc|2rdacarrier \n500    Title from label mounted on box. \n500    \"Book one is an archival letterpress-printed, laser cut \n       accordion artists' book printed during a letterpress \n       studio arts residency at Women's Studio Workshop in \n       Rosendale, NY. The book uses 11 handset type faces from \n       the studio's historically-rich collection to present a \n       variety of voices. The book expresses, in each survivor's \n       own words, the beginning of each survivor's experience. \n       The image of the original jar developed from a photograph \n       into a photo-polymer plate serves as the main artwork. The\n       book is laser cut to give the illusion of slips of paper \n       floating inside a jar with seemingly endless depth. \n       Looking at the book straight on, the stories begin to \n       build, filling the jar both visually and conceptually. The\n       sculptural format of the book makes reference not only to \n       the appalling frequency of rape (an American is sexually \n       assaulted every 107 seconds) but also hints at the \n       complications which arise from viewing sexual assault as a\n       vast, entangled body versus a collection of interconnected\n       individual experiences that share similarities and \n       differences that reveal opportunities for advocacy. The \n       book's laser cut layout was tested at 3-Scan Labs in San \n       Francisco and the final cutting performed at Crashspace in\n       Los Angeles. The book is bound in green Brillianta book \n       cloth covered boards and stored in a slipcase. Colophon on\n       end paper.\"--Artist's website. \n500    \"Book two uses the flag book structure developed by Hedi \n       Kyle, where slips of paper jut across each other to create\n       the impression of multiple, layered voices passing over \n       and through each other. The book contains words and \n       phrases in the survivors' own words describing the assault\n       itself. The book is printed on archival quality \n       translucent photo papers embodying transparent text and \n       imagery of a broken jar. A letterpress printed spine and \n       end papers printed at LALA Press [in Los Angeles, CA] with\n       a hard cover of Asahi book cloth covered boards complete \n       the book's layers of graphic images, transparency, and \n       texture. Colophon on back cover.\"--Artist's website. \n500    \"Book three is a codex hand-bound book with a handmade \n       paper cover containing raw silk and blue glass inclusions \n       (sealed for archival and handling purposes). The pages, \n       letterpress printed at KALA Arts Institute [in Berkeley, \n       CA], juxtapose pressure prints and type to convey the \n       thoughts and reflections of each survivor at the time they\n       submitted their narrative. Each book is bound by hand with\n       blue wax thread. Colophon on inside of back cover.\"--\n       Artist's website. \n500    Condition: no library markings, in protective enclosure. \n520    \"Jarring III is a set of three letterpress printed & hand-\n       bound artists' books in an edition of 50 that seek to end \n       the silence and stigma surrounding sexual assault and rape\n       by sharing the narratives of 22 survivors. The goals of \n       the project are as follows: Promote discourse and \n       awareness about sexual assault in our communities; Speak \n       out about sexual assault by sharing the experiences of \n       sexual assault survivors; Crea